The member initializers already copy each field directly, and `FieldBase`'s internals aren't visible here, so there is no safe change that would be measurably faster. The rewrite only makes the base-class copy explicit with a `static_cast`. Behavior and generated code should be identical, so don't expect a speedup from this change.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(static_cast<const FieldBase &>(field))
    , profile(field.profile)
    , profileIndex(field.profileIndex)
    , type(field.type)
    , isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
}
```